This problem is to determine if a move made in a simple curses based
video game was made by a expert player, or was a random move.  The
data was collected by recording the moves made by a human player, and
later recording the moves made by a random player.  The total
collection of moves was then randomly split to get a training/test
partition.

Each move is defined by the direction taken (n,s,e,w) and by the
contents of all squares within distance one of the current square.
The content of a square is one of the values

 stone - obstacle
 money - increases score 
 floor - empty space 
 g_trl - trail of agent
 h_trl - trail of 'hunter'
 mgrub - agent 
 hunter - an autonomous opponent that must be avoided.
